 ],
 "literal": "What is this, O friend? In the seashore grove where birds chirp and ancient ocean waves splash, / under the shade of the sand dune near the blooming flower clusters of the Punnai tree, / at the time when our secret tryst succeeded, / my eyes indeed saw the lord of the shore, / my ears indeed heard his words; / but when uniting with him, they attain great beauty, / and when parting from him, my broad, soft shoulders slip loose.",
 "translation": "What is this, my friend? In the seashore grove where birds chirp and ancient ocean waves splash, under the shade of the sand dune near the blooming Punnai tree, when our secret tryst succeeded, my eyes saw the lord of the shore and my ears heard his words. But now, while they gain great beauty when we are united, my broad, soft shoulders grow thin and waste away whenever he departs.",
 "modern": "தோழியே! இது என்ன? பழமையான கடல் அலைகள் வந்து மோதும், பறவைகள் ஒலிக்கும் கடற்கரைச் சோலையில், கொத்துக் கொத்தாக மலர்கள் மலர்ந்த புன்னை மரத்தின் நிழலில், மணல் மேட்டில் நம்முடைய சந்திப்பு நிகழ்ந்தபோது, என் கண்கள் அந்தத் தலைவனைக் கண்டன; என் காதுகள் அவனுடைய சொற்களைக் கேட்டன. ஆனால், அவனோடு கூடி இருக்கும்போது மிகுந்த அழகைப் பெறும் என் பருத்த மென்மையான தோள்கள், அவன் பிரிந்து செல்லும்போது மெலிந்து வளைகள் கழலுகின்றனவே!",
 "explanation": "The heroine is speaking to her close friend about her distress during temporary separations from her lover. She recalls the sweet moments of their secret meetings in the coastal grove under the shade of the blooming Punnai tree, where her eyes saw him and her ears heard his comforting words. However, she laments the physical toll of separation, noting that her shoulders flourish in his presence but waste away when he leaves. This poem belongs to the Neytal (coastal) landscape, where the sea, sand dunes, and Punnai trees form the backdrop for themes of longing and separation. The physical thinning of the heroine's shoulders is a classic motif representing her deep emotional distress.",
